## Method

score = {{ weights.demand }}·Demand + {{ weights.entry }}·Entry + {{ weights.gap }}·Gap + {{ weights.price }}·Price − {{ weights.crowding }}·Crowding, each a percentile across this run's niches over the {{ top_n }} most favourited listings per niche (from the top search results for each seed).

- Demand: the average of {% if blended %}three{% else %}two{% endif %} percentiles: favourite momentum (each listing's favourites divided by its age in months, at least 1, summed){% if blended %}, reviews in the last {{ window }} days, and favourites gained since the previous run{% else %} and reviews in the last {{ window }} days{% endif %}. Niches below the {{ (floor * 100)|int }}th demand percentile are dropped.
- Entry: share of favourite momentum on listings under {{ new_days }} days old.
- Gap: complaints a better template would fix, per 100 reviews.
- Price: median listing price (USD).
- Crowding: total listings for the niche's keywords, and the top 3 shops' share of favourite momentum.
- Confidence: high when at least {{ min_listings }} of the top listings have {{ min_favourites }}+ favourites; high-confidence niches rank above low-confidence ones.

These are proxies: favourites and reviews are not sales, so the report ranks niches against each other and does not estimate sales.
